  "question": {
    "text": "A wave disturbance in a medium is described by $y(x, t)=0.02 \\cos \\left(50 \\pi t+\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\cos (10 \\pi x)$ where $x, y$ are in meters and $t$ is in second. Which statement(s) is/are correct?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "A node occurs at $x=0.15 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "An antinode occurs at $x=0.3 \\mathrm{~m}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "The speed of the wave is $4 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{sec}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "The wavelength of the wave is 0.2 m",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\cos 10 \\pi x=0 \\rightarrow$ Node\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& 10 \\pi \\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{n} \\pi+\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\\\\n& 10 \\pi \\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{n} \\pi+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{x}=0, \\frac{1}{20} \\mathrm{~m}, \\frac{3}{20} \\mathrm{~m} \\\\\n& \\cos \\pi \\mathrm{x}= \\pm 1 \\rightarrow \\text { Antinode } \\\\\n& 10 \\pi \\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{n} \\pi, \\mathrm{x}=0, \\frac{1}{10} \\mathrm{~m}, \\frac{2}{10} \\mathrm{~m}, \\frac{3}{10} \\mathrm{~m} \\\\\n& \\text { wave speed }(\\mathrm{v})=\\frac{\\omega}{\\mathrm{k}}=\\frac{50 \\pi}{10 \\pi}=5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}, \\mathrm{k}=10 \\pi, \\frac{2 \\pi}{\\lambda}=10 \\pi, \\lambda=\\frac{2}{10}=0.2 \\mathrm{~m}\n\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}